    <name>Parallel Consumer - Proxy Client Java API</name>
    <artifactId>parallel-consumer-proxy-client-java-api</artifactId>

    <!--
        The shared Java wrapper surface: the API both transports implement and the nine other
        languages mirror, plus the transport-parameterised conformance suite in this module's
        test-jar (astubbs#242, the plan's U29 spike; U20 grows the suite to the full set).

        DEPENDENCY-FREE, deliberately: every arrow points INTO this module (api <- direct,
        api <- grpc), and nothing here may depend on core, the protocol module, protobuf or gRPC.
        Transport types must never appear on this surface; the direct sibling's bannedDependencies
        rule is what makes that checkable - a transport type leaking in here fails THAT module's
        build. The test tree is bound by the same rule, because the test-jar lands on the direct
        module's test classpath.
    -->

</project>
